<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE TREE

  What a city's keepers can work out for themselves, and what working it out opens.

  A node's WHOLE EFFECT is minting a roster key. `Grants="node:kiln"` is the same kind of string
  a taught data disk and a certified machine already write, and the same `Knowledge=` gate on a
  <building> matches it. So a third party gates their building on their own research with one
  attribute in their own KingdomBuildings.xml and no C# at all, and every one of the catalogue's
  existing gates keeps working untouched.

  Every entry answers these, and all of them are optional but Key:

    Key        Registry identity. A later file re-using a Key owns that node whole, exactly as it
               does for a <building>.
    DisplayName How the founder reads it. Falls back to the Key.
    Branch     Which spine it hangs on. A free string, so a mod adds a fourth.
    Tier       1-4. Each tier is an Intelligence threshold on the CITY's best researcher, never on
               the founder: 10 / 14 / 18 / 22. Hard at the boundary and soft inside it - below the
               threshold the subject cannot be taken up at all, and above it a better mind only
               makes the work faster. Tier 4 sits deliberately above what settlers roll, which is
               why the top of a city's tree is reached through a PERSON: a lodged savant, or
               somebody found in the world and asked.
    Requires   Roster tokens, ALL required, in exactly the grammar `Knowledge=` already speaks -
               `node:`, `disk:`, `machine:`, `origin:`, `creed:`, `pattern:`, `rite:`, and a `|`
               inside one token for "any of these".
    MinTech    Craft rung the CITY must have reached. Per city now, so a second city walks its own
               ladder.
    Grants     Roster keys minted on completion. Defaults to `node:<Key>`.
    Effort     Staff-days of thinking a fully-crewed bench takes.
    Reveals    Nodes made visible on completion - filtered through admissibility first, so a road
               this city can never walk is never offered and is never mentioned.
    TaughtBy   Tokens that grant this outright with no bench time: a disk read to the keepers, a
               treatise. A `rite:` token here is a LOAD ERROR, not a convention.
    SeededBy   Tokens that REVEAL this and BEGIN it at a head start, and can never finish it.
               Every `rite:` token lives here. A rite opens a door; the city walks through.
    Forbidden  Tokens that make this node invisible and unreachable, told to nobody - and told to
               nobody in exactly the way an undiscovered node is, so the two cannot be told apart.
    Quest      A vanilla quest, or `Quest~Step`, that must be finished before this node EXISTS.
    Effect     `efficiency:N` (the realm-wide method lane, capped at +50 however many grant it),
               `statcap:<Stat>:N` (how far above what they walked in with this city may teach a
               citizen - capped at +1 for Intelligence, never stacking, and +3 for anything else),
               `recruitreveal:N` (the city begins hearing of people worth sending for).

  THE VISIBILITY LAW governs every surface that reads this file. You see what you have unlocked;
  you do not see what you have not; you especially cannot see what you CAN'T. There is no greyed
  row, no silhouette, and no count of the unseen anywhere - which is vanilla's own rule for an
  unknown tinker recipe, not one we invented.

  TWO LADDERS. This tree is NOT the craft ladder. A node is worth zero craft points; craft still
  rises by disks taught and machines certified, exactly as it did before the tree existed.
-->
<kingdomresearch>

  <!-- ======================================================================== THE TRUNK ==
    Three nodes everybody walks, and the first of them is the keystone: until somebody here
    writes anything down there is no map of what the keepers know, because nobody is keeping
    one. The map is not a screen the founder is given. It is a thing the keepers begin to draw.
  -->
  <node Key="notekeeping" DisplayName="note-keeping" Branch="trunk" Tier="1"
        Grants="node:notes" Effort="4"
        Reveals="node:measuredwork,node:apprenticeship,node:salvagesense,node:butchery,node:themoot" />

  <node Key="measuredwork" DisplayName="measured work" Branch="trunk" Tier="1"
        Requires="node:notes" Grants="node:measuredwork" Effort="6"
        Effect="efficiency:5" Reveals="node:schooling" />

  <node Key="apprenticeship" DisplayName="apprenticeship" Branch="trunk" Tier="2"
        Requires="node:notes" Grants="node:apprenticeship" Effort="8"
        Effect="statcap:any:1" Reveals="node:schooling,node:physic" />

  <!-- ==================================================================== THE FOUNDRY ==
    Materials, works, power. The branch that makes certification mean something: somebody had to
    find a furnace, claim the ground it stands on or haul one home, and pay for it to go on the
    grid, before the keepers could be taught to smelt. Certification already ships and gates
    exactly one design today; this branch is why it exists.
  -->
  <node Key="salvagesense" DisplayName="salvage sense" Branch="foundry" Tier="1"
        Requires="node:notes" Grants="node:salvagesense" Effort="6"
        Reveals="node:kilnheat" />

  <node Key="kilnheat" DisplayName="kiln heat" Branch="foundry" Tier="2"
        Requires="node:salvagesense" MinTech="Salvage" Grants="node:kiln" Effort="10"
        Effect="efficiency:5" Reveals="node:cruciblesteel" />

  <node Key="cruciblesteel" DisplayName="crucible steel" Branch="foundry" Tier="3"
        Requires="node:kiln,machine:Glass Furnace" MinTech="Foundry" Grants="node:cruciblesteel"
        Effort="14"
        Reveals="node:pressurevessels,node:powerlattice" />

  <node Key="pressurevessels" DisplayName="pressure vessels" Branch="foundry" Tier="3"
        Requires="node:cruciblesteel" Grants="node:pressure" Effort="14"
        Reveals="node:arclightdiscipline" />

  <node Key="powerlattice" DisplayName="the power lattice" Branch="foundry" Tier="3"
        Requires="node:cruciblesteel" Grants="node:lattice" Effort="16"
        Effect="efficiency:5" TaughtBy="disk:Arc Winder"
        Reveals="node:arclightdiscipline" />

  <node Key="arclightdiscipline" DisplayName="arclight discipline" Branch="foundry" Tier="4"
        Requires="node:lattice,node:pressure" MinTech="Arclight" Grants="node:arclight"
        Effort="30" SeededBy="rite:Barathrumites"
        Reveals="node:therolls" />

  <!-- The chrome half of the body doctrine (Addendum 22 A1; END-STATE §2.3, §7.4). True Kin
       is a matter of RECORD: this node is the city working out how to keep its own. A Templar
       city never sees it - the visibility law at full strength, same as the vat. -->
  <node Key="therolls" DisplayName="the rolls" Branch="foundry" Tier="4"
        Requires="node:arclight" MinTech="Arclight" Grants="node:rolls" Effort="30"
        SeededBy="rite:Mechanimists" Forbidden="creed:Templar" />

  <!-- ====================================================================== THE FLESH ==
    Bodies, medicine, and what a city may teach the people who live in it. The vat is the
    visibility law's hard case and the reason it is written down: a city that holds with the
    Templar must never see that it exists - not greyed, not counted in a tail, not named in a
    roads-not-taken line.
  -->
  <node Key="butchery" DisplayName="butchery" Branch="flesh" Tier="1"
        Requires="node:notes" Grants="node:butchery" Effort="6"
        Reveals="node:thevat,node:physic" />

  <node Key="thevat" DisplayName="the vat" Branch="flesh" Tier="2"
        Requires="node:butchery" Grants="node:vat" Effort="12"
        SeededBy="rite:Oozes,rite:Fungi" Forbidden="creed:Templar"
        Reveals="node:thelongdraught,node:thegraft" />

  <node Key="physic" DisplayName="physic" Branch="flesh" Tier="2"
        Requires="node:butchery,node:apprenticeship" Grants="node:physic" Effort="12"
        Effect="statcap:Toughness:1" Reveals="node:thelongdraught" />

  <node Key="thelongdraught" DisplayName="the long draught" Branch="flesh" Tier="3"
        Requires="node:physic,node:vat" Grants="node:longdraught" Effort="18"
        Effect="statcap:Strength:1,statcap:Agility:1" />

  <node Key="thegraft" DisplayName="the graft" Branch="flesh" Tier="3"
        Requires="node:vat" MinTech="Foundry" Grants="node:graft" Effort="22"
        Reveals="node:chimerism" />

  <node Key="chimerism" DisplayName="chimerism" Branch="flesh" Tier="4"
        Requires="node:graft" MinTech="Arclight" Grants="node:chimerism" Effort="30"
        SeededBy="rite:Girsh" />

  <!-- ====================================================================== THE CHOIR ==
    Mind, teaching, and the city's ear. This is the branch that feeds research back into
    research, and the one place a runaway could hide - which is why schooling's grant is
    capped at a single point of Intelligence and cannot stack with anything, ours or anyone
    else's.
  -->
  <node Key="themoot" DisplayName="the moot" Branch="choir" Tier="1"
        Requires="node:notes" Grants="node:moot" Effort="6"
        Reveals="node:thecensus,node:schooling,node:thequietcell" />

  <node Key="thecensus" DisplayName="the census" Branch="choir" Tier="2"
        Requires="node:notes,node:moot" Grants="node:census" Effort="10"
        Effect="recruitreveal:1" />

  <node Key="schooling" DisplayName="schooling" Branch="choir" Tier="2"
        Requires="node:moot,node:apprenticeship" Grants="node:schooling" Effort="14"
        Effect="efficiency:10,statcap:Intelligence:1" />

  <node Key="thequietcell" DisplayName="the quiet cell" Branch="choir" Tier="2"
        Requires="node:moot" Grants="node:quiet" Effort="12"
        SeededBy="rite:Seekers,rite:Chavvah" Forbidden="creed:Templar,creed:Mechanimists"
        Reveals="node:thelisteninghall" />

  <node Key="thelisteninghall" DisplayName="the listening hall" Branch="choir" Tier="3"
        Requires="node:quiet" MinTech="Workshop" Grants="node:listening" Effort="18"
        Reveals="node:assent" />

  <node Key="assent" DisplayName="assent" Branch="choir" Tier="4"
        Requires="node:listening" Grants="node:assent" Effort="30"
        SeededBy="rite:Chavvah" />

</kingdomresearch>
